Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> Is there a NetHack wiki anywhere out there? I've checked Google but it only
> brings up the Wikipedia entry on NetHack.

As mastercontrol and Grunt have pointed out, yes, there is one, at
http://nethack.wikia.com/.

> Also considering the vast amount of spoilage out there, Dylan's Gazetteer,
> Steelypips, Eva's site and www.nicolaas.net/erebus/ would a NetHack based
> wiki just add noise rather than signal?

Not necessarily. For one, all of those pages you mentioned are not
directly editable by the community, the defining feature of a wiki
(with a wiki there's a much much smaller barrier to contribution of a
new idea). Secondly, the spoilers are mostly just translations of the
NetHack source. The wiki includes (again, user-editable) strategy
pages, such as

http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Dig_for_victory

You don't see DfV documented on any of the pages you mentioned because
it's a relatively new technique (no more than a few months old). Also,
the wiki supports direct links to the source code (which is given in
annotatable wiki pages) so people can verify for themselves that the
information is accurate.

Check out the article on Mjollnir, for example (
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Mjollnir ). None of your pages give such
an in-depth look at Mojo, or if they do, the information is probably
spread widely.

So there is definitely a niche for a NetHack wiki.

